diations (Byrd order)\r\n 14: \r\n 15: ### R1. Replace placeholder client FRs with testable AC\r\n 16: \r\n 17: **FAIL:** wiki/MCP exports still have \"Placeholder requirement backfilled\" for FR-AUTH-001, FR-AUTH-002, FR-SYS-001, FR-PLT-001, FR-ROM-001..004, FR-TASK-001/002. Mappings omit those IDs. No TEST-AUTH record.\r\n 18: \r\n 19: **Work:**\r\n 20: 1. Update each FR in MCP (`workspacePath` `F:\\GitHub\\RomM`) with real body + numbered AC (Bearer `rmm_`, Basic, OAuth refresh skew, 401/403 types, heartbeat schema, platforms list/get, roms page fields, pagination).\r\n 21: 2. Create TEST-AUTH, TEST-SYS, TEST-PLT, TEST-ROM covering those AC by test class/method.\r\n 22: 3. Create mappings FR -> TR-AUTH-001 / TR-HTTP-001 / TR-ROMM-API-001 -> TEST-*.\r\n 23: 4. Export wiki. Placeholder text must be gone.\r\n 24: \r\n 25: **Exit:** `requirements_list` shows non-placeholder bodies; TR-per-FR-Mapping lists FR-AUTH-001/002 and FR-ROM-00x; TEST-AUTH exists.\r\n 26: \r\n 27: ### R2. Heartbeat contract vs OpenAPI 5.0.0\r\n 28: \r\n 29: **FAIL:** pinned `openapi/romm-5.0.0.json` nests heartbeat fields under `SYSTEM`. Client `HeartbeatResponse` and test fixtures use top-level `Version` / `ShowSetupWizard`. A conforming server response deserializes those as null.\r\n 30: \r\n 31: **Work:**\r\n 32: 1. Write a failing test that deserializes a `SYSTEM`-wrapped fixture and asserts Version/ShowSetupWizard (or documents the mapped property).\r\n 33: 2. Change the model/JSON mapping to match OpenAPI (nested SYSTEM or explicit JsonPropertyName path).\r\n 34: 3. Keep a negative test that a top-level-only fixture is not silently treated as the live contract.\r\n 35: \r\n 36: **Files:** `src/RomM.Client/Models/CoreModels.cs` (HeartbeatResponse), `tests/RomM.Client.Tests/RomMCoreClientTests.cs`, `openapi/romm-5.0.0.json`.\r\n 37: \r\n 38: ### R3. OpenAPI coverage must not auto-pass `/api/*`\r\n 39: \r\n 40: **FAIL:** coverage test accepts every `/api/*` path, so PASS does not prove the operation is implemented.\r\n 41: \r\n 42: **Work:**\r\n 43: 1. Change `OpenApiCoverageTests` / `OpenApiPathCoverage` so unmapped `/api/*` paths FAIL or are an explicit allow-list with a comment and TEST-SPEC-001 AC.\r\n 44: 2. Phase 2 scope: heartbeat, platforms, roms list/get, pagination query params must be mapped to real client methods.\r\n 45: \r\n 46: **Files:** `src/RomM.Client/OpenApiPathCoverage.cs`, `tests/RomM.Client.Tests/OpenApiCoverageTests.cs`.\r\n 47: \r\n 48: ### R4. Credential leakage on absolute URLs\r\n 49: \r\n 50: **FAIL (security):** public transport attaches the configured Bearer token to an absolute URL on another host. OAuth sends username/password to that host's `/api/token`.\r\n 51: \r\n 52: **Work:**\r\n 53: 1. Red tests: `SendAsync` to `https://evil.example/api/roms` must not include `Authorization` from the RomM client; OAuth must not POST secrets to a non-base host.\r\n 54: 2. Restrict auth injection to the configured `BaseAddress` host (and relative URIs). Refuse or strip auth on cross-host absolute URIs unless explicitly opted in.\r\n 55: 3. Same-origin check for OAuth token endpoint (already `/api/token` on request URI; pin to BaseAddress).\r\n 56: \r\n 57: **Files:** `src/RomM.Client/Http/RomMTransport.cs`, `src/RomM.Client/Auth/RomMAuthHandler.cs`, `tests/RomM.Client.Tests/RomMAuthHandlerTests.cs`, `tests/RomM.Client.Tests/RomMHttpExceptionMappingTests.cs`.\r\n 58: \r\n 59: ### R5. Pagination early termination\r\n 60: \r\n 61: **FAIL:** `EnumerateAsync` (or equivalent) stops paging too early vs `total`/`offset`/`limit`.\r\n 62: \r\n 63: **Work:**\r\n 64: 1. Red test: server total=3, limit=1, three pages; enumerator must yield 3 items.\r\n 65: 2. Fix loop to continue until offset+count >= total or a short page with no next.\r\n 66: \r\n 67: **Files:** `src/RomM.Client/Clients/ResourceClients.cs`, `tests/RomM.Client.Tests/RomListQueryTests.cs`, `RomMCoreClientTests.cs`.\r\n 68: \r\n 69: ### R6. Cancellation: no yield after cancel\r\n 70: \r\n 71: **FAIL:** enumerator yielded an item after cancellation.\r\n 72: \r\n 73: **Work:**\r\n 74: 1. Red test: cancel after first page; no further `MoveNext` success.\r\n 75: 2. Check `cancellationToken` before each yield and before the next HTTP call.\r\n 76: \r\n 77: **Files:** `ResourceClients.cs` `EnumerateAsync`.\r\n 78: \r\n 79: ### R7. Task/scan payloads vs pinned schema\r\n 80: \r\n 81: **FAIL:** task responses fail against the pinned OpenAPI schema (phase 2 adjacent if scan is in iteration 2; if scan is iteration 3, still fix before claiming ROM I/O complete).\r\n 82: \r\n 83: **Work:**\r\n 84: 1. Compare `TaskInfo` / `TaskExecutionResponse` / `TaskStatusResponse` to `openapi/romm-5.0.0.json`.\r\n 85: 2. Red tests with fixtures from the spec; then fix DTOs.\r\n 86: \r\n 87: **Files:** `CoreModels.cs`, `ResourceClients.cs` tasks client, `RomMCoreClientTests.cs`.\r\n 88: \r\n 89: ## Non-blocking but recorded\r\n 90: \r\n 91: - Concurrent OAuth shares one grant: PASS (keep a regression test).\r\n 92: - Rejected refresh clears token store: PASS (keep a regression test).\r\n 93: - Native Codex sandbox exec 206 on this host: use PowerShell.MCP for agent test runs; do not treat as a product defect.\r\n 94: - Live MCP reads failed under `approval_policy=never` in the first Codex exec. Re-verify R1 against MCP `requirements_list` after R1, not only wiki files.\r\n 95: \r\n 96: ## Exit for phases 1 and 2\r\n 97: \r\n 98: 1. R1 wiki/MCP placeholders gone; TEST-AUTH mapped.\r\n 99: 2. R2-R6 red-then-green; focused `RomM.Client.Tests` 0 fail 0 skip.\r\n100: 3. Hostile AGREE on Iteration 1 and Iteration 2 claims (not Codex babysit unless you ask).\r\n101: 4. Only then keep IMPL-ROMMCLIENT-001 / Iteration 2 `Done=true` with a new DoneSummary citing the new tests.\r\n102: \r\n103: Do not treat the existing 46/46 green run as closing these phases.\r\ntests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\RomMHttpExceptionMappingTests.cs\r\ntests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\RomMCoreClientTests.cs\r\ntests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\RomMClientOptionsTests.cs\r\ntests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\RomMAuthHandlerTests.cs\r\ntests\\RomM.Client.Tests\\RomM.Client.Tests.csproj\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\OpenApiPathCoverage.cs\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\Clients\\ResourceClients.cs\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\Models\\CoreModels.cs\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\Auth\\RomMAuthHandler.cs\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\Auth\\RomMAuth.cs\r\nsrc\\RomM.Client\\Exceptions\\RomMAuthException.cs"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
